          "entities": {},
          "text": "Over the past 250 million years, shifting tectonic plates and volcanic activity transformed the Dolomites from ancient coral reefs into the dramatic mountain range we see today.\n\nThough the landscape is now defined by towering peaks, traces of its underwater origins remain preserved in fossils of marine life such as bivalves and ammonites. These remnants also reveal that the reef systems that once formed the Dolomites supported thriving microbial communities, likely including cyanobacteria a powerful reminder that landscapes are never fixed, but continually shaped and reshaped over time. What we see today is simply their most recent evolution."
